            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0248" n="136" xml:id="pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 551/42.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>,<date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-06-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 19,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Rockhill states that he has been officially informed by the foreign office
                    that the customs-houses will be opened on July 1, at Dairen and Antung, with a
                    branch house at Tatungkou.)</p>
            </div>
